Third-party datasets redistributed in this repository
=====================================================

This repository redistributes the annotation files of two public
benchmark datasets so that the results reported in the PlotPick paper can
be reproduced exactly. For ChartX this is every record of both splits (6000
entries: the 1152-entry test split with all its fields, and the
4848-entry validation split reduced to the image name, chart type, title
and CSV table the benchmark reads); for PlotQA it is a 1000-entry subset
of the test split. No chart images are redistributed; they are fetched from the
original sources by pipeline/fetch_chartx_images.py.

Licence texts are in LICENSES/.

ChartX
------
Files: external/chartx/chartx_test.json, external/chartx/chartx_val.json
Copyright: the ChartX authors (Shanghai AI Laboratory and collaborators)
Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/InternScience/ChartX
Licence: Apache-2.0
Citation: Xia et al., "ChartX & ChartVLM: A Versatile Benchmark and
  Foundation Model for Complicated Chart Reasoning", arXiv:2402.12185.

The copies here are MODIFIED: ground-truth errors found during evaluation
(CSV columns not shown in the chart, errors in the redrawing code, and
stacked-bar annotations giving totals instead of segment values) were
corrected in eight test-split figures. The corrections are
listed in external/chartx/CORRECTIONS.md so that the modifications are
identifiable, as Apache-2.0 section 4(b) requires.

PlotQA
------
Files: external/plotqa_test_1000.json, external/plotqa_test_100.json
Source: https://github.com/NiteshMethani/PlotQA
Licence: CC-BY-4.0 (dataset), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Citation: Methani, Ganguly, Khapra and Kumar, "PlotQA: Reasoning over
  Scientific Plots", WACV 2020.
These files are a subset of the PlotQA test split, adapted into the field
layout this benchmark reads. They are provided without warranties, as
CC-BY-4.0 section 5 sets out.

Not redistributed
-----------------
Subsets of ChartQA, ChartQAPro and ChartMuseum were used in exploratory
work that is not reported in the paper. They are not included here
because their redistribution terms were not established. The scripts that
reference them remain, and will not run until that data is obtained from
the original sources.

PubMed Central content
----------------------
results/pmc/, reports/, pairs.json, candidates.csv and excluded_pairs.json
contain values and metadata from figures and tables in PubMed Central
Open Access Subset articles, identified by PMCID. Each
source article carries its own licence; consult the article record before
reusing its content. No patient-identifiable data is included; all values
are aggregate figures as published.

Derived values
--------------
The result files under results/ and the summaries under reports/ embed
ground-truth values copied from ChartX and PlotQA, so the terms above
apply to them as well.
